  "full_text": "So the next day, when I went to get on the bus, they didn't let me board and they like ripped up my ticket. I was like, oh, I'm a prisoner or something. So I was there for another couple days and then I walked out of the gorge 80 miles and then hitchhiked to Tri-Cities. But anyway, when I was about to leave, this dude comes up and elbows me in the face. But it was really weird. It hit me like right between the nose and mouth. It didn't break any teeth and it didn't bloody my nose. And it was like it just stopped. It was like, that was weird. My head jerked back. My head just jerked back, but I took the punch. I took it. I was like, well, that's kind of weird. I wonder if I'm like Superman or something. I don't know what happened. Because that should have knocked me. It should have done worse. I wonder if he pulled his punch. I don't know. It seemed like he fucking elbowed me.",
